Subject: Compile the monolith bodies of chain-run opcodes out of threaded builds

What this does
  In a threaded register build, wraps the `js_regvm_execute` `L_ROP_*` body of
  every opcode the threaded chain runs in `#if !QJS_REGVM_THREAD`, and points
  their `regvm_dispatch` entries at one `L_mono_unreachable` trap that aborts.
  Kept: the `REGVM_T_FALLBACK_LIST` opcodes (the loop is their executor),
  `call`/`call_method` (the loop runs them when `QJS_REGVM_RECORD=0`), and
  `return`, `return_undefined`, `tail_call`, `tail_call_method`, whose handlers
  hand a generator frame back to the loop. Macro definitions inside the
  wrapped regions stay outside the guards, since the step engine and the cold
  arms use them. `pic` is declared only where its readers are compiled.

Why we need it
  The loop enters the chain whenever `regvm_is_threaded[*rpc]`, so in a
  threaded build those bodies cannot run, yet they were compiled into every
  register binary: 199 dispatch labels of dead code.

What it adds
  `REGVM_MONO_ENTRY` and the trap label. Monolith builds (`QJS_REGVM_THREAD=0`,
  `QJS_AOT`, `QJS_REGVM_STEPCHECK`) preprocess to the same tokens as before.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

